  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Soft marine retail demand drove same-store sales declines, exacerbated by a boat show timing shift and the divestiture of a non-core chemicals subsidiary. External conditions remain challenging for big-ticket discretionary purchases. Positively, a richer mix of higher-margin new and pre-owned boats lifted gross profitability, indicating a quality-over-quantity shift despite the volume headwinds.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is actively reshaping the portfolio, using the Ocean Bio-Chem sale to significantly pay down debt and reduce leverage. The focus has pivoted to margin expansion through disciplined pricing and a more focused brand mix, rather than chasing revenue. Management maintained its full-year guidance, signaling confidence in the strategic direction, even as a non-cash impairment charge widened the reported net loss.",
